Extra firewall rules go here, in files ending in .nft.

/etc/nftables.conf loads these last, so they are appended to its chains and are
not touched by an image update.

The input chain drops by default, so a rule only needs to accept:

    # /etc/nftables.d/10-snmp.nft
    add rule inet appliance input iif "eth0" udp dport 161 accept

To limit a routing protocol to one interface, remove the broad rule from the
routing chain and put a narrower one here.

Check before applying, a mistake here can lock you out of SSH:

    nft --check --file /etc/nftables.conf
    systemctl reload nftables
